# Copy to .env for local development. On Vercel, set these under
# Project -> Settings -> Environment Variables.
#
# .env* is gitignored — never commit real values.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where the used cars come from
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The cars live in the website's OWN database: the `used_cars` table in the
# Supabase project configured further down (NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL and
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY — both REQUIRED for the stock, see that section).
# Cars are added and edited in /admin, photos go to the `car-photos` bucket of
# the same project. The table and bucket are created by
# supabase/migrations/20261114120000_used_cars.sql, which has to be applied to
# that project once.
#
# The public pages switch over by themselves (lib/inventory/server.ts):
#   - table missing or completely empty  -> stock is read from WordPress
#   - table holds at least one car       -> the database is the only source;
#                                           WordPress is no longer consulted
#   - table exists but cannot be read    -> pages show "stock list is not
#                                           loading" rather than fall back to
#                                           WordPress and re-list sold cars
#
# The stock is also served as JSON, public and read-only:
#   GET /api/vehicles            cars on sale; takes the same filters as
#                                /inventory (make, model, bodyType, fuel,
#                                transmission, condition, budget, priceMin,
#                                priceMax, year, kmsMax, q, sort) plus
#                                limit (max 100) and offset
#   GET /api/vehicles/<id>       one car, by number or by page slug
#   GET /api/feed/meta           the Meta (Facebook / Instagram) catalogue feed
# The two /api/vehicles responses carry a `source` field: "database" or
# "wordpress".
# /api/inventory/used is a different thing: a raw view of the WordPress sync,
# kept for checking the import. It is not what the site shows.

# WordPress — the stock is only read from it UNTIL the cars have been imported
# into the database. This is the origin of the WordPress site the old listings
# are read from (lib/integrations/motors). next.config.ts also takes the
# hostname from it to decide which host car photographs may be loaded from, so
# keep it correct for as long as any car's photos are still served by
# WordPress.
#
# While WordPress still owns amgroupind.com you can leave this unset. If DNS
# points amgroupind.com at Vercel BEFORE the import has run you MUST set it to
# wherever WordPress has moved, or the sync will request inventory from this
# app itself, find no Motors markup, and the site will render zero cars.
#
# MOTORS_BASE_URL=https://legacy.amgroupind.com

# Optional shared secret enabling the ?fresh=1 cache bypass on
# /api/inventory/used. Without it the bypass is simply unavailable.
# MOTORS_REFRESH_TOKEN=

# Public address of this site, no trailing slash. Car links in /api/vehicles,
# the sitemap and structured data are built from it and fall back to
# https://amgroupind.com when it is unset. The Meta feed uses it too, but falls
# back to the address the feed was requested on instead. Set it in production
# so every one of them agrees.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://amgroupind.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Admin area (REQUIRED)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# /admin exposes every lead's name, phone and email. Use a long random value —
# NOT the local development password.
ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# Signs the admin session cookie. Any long random string; rotating it logs
# everyone out. Generate with:  openssl rand -base64 32
ADMIN_SESSION_SECRET=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase — the used cars AND lead storage (REQUIRED in production)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# One project holds both the `used_cars` table (with the `car-photos` bucket)
# and the `leads` table.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL + SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY are what the stock is
# read and written with. The service-role key is used on the server only and
# must never be given a NEXT_PUBLIC_ name. Without the pair the site behaves as
# if the cars table did not exist: the public pages keep reading WordPress and
# cars cannot be saved from /admin.
#
# Without these, leads also fall back to a local file store, which does not
# persist on Vercel: every deploy discards them.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Lead emails — every enquiry is also emailed, so one reaches a person even if
# the database is down. Leave SMTP_* empty to turn emails off.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The mailbox that SENDS the email (e.g. a no-reply@ mailbox at your host).
SMTP_HOST=
SMTP_PORT=465
SMTP_USER=
SMTP_PASS=
# Who receives enquiries (comma-separated) and the From address.
LEADS_EMAIL_TO=aryan@amgroupind.com, data@amgroupind.com
LEADS_EMAIL_FROM=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Media library (SECOND Supabase project — photos only, no lead data)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The `am_group_files` photo bucket lives in a different project from the one
# above. Kept separate on purpose: this project only ever needs public read, so
# it must not be reachable with the service-role key that can read `leads`.
#
# Objects in the bucket are publicly readable, so images RENDER without a key.
# The key is only needed to LIST the bucket — Supabase requires auth for that.
# Without it, /gallery falls back to the curated paths in lib/media/storage.ts
# and says so on the page; with it, the whole library appears automatically.
#
# Use the ANON key, not the service-role key.
MEDIA_SUPABASE_URL=https://ehcmjypfxucvcvuofozx.supabase.co
MEDIA_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Analytics
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google Tag Manager container, e.g. GTM-XXXXXXX. GTM does not load at all
# while this is empty.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GTM_ID=

# Load GTM in development too. Off by default so local traffic does not
# pollute production analytics.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GTM_DEV=true

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Contact
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WhatsApp number in digits only, with country code and no "+". Must be a
# number actually registered on WhatsApp, or every WhatsApp button opens a
# dead "phone number shared via url is invalid" screen. Defaults to the
# primary showroom number in lib/locations.ts.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_WHATSAPP_NUMBER=919419100000
